From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Resync the series with the tree that builds libvulkan.prx.

0001-0040 no longer rebuilt the driver that shipped from 01.38 to 01.40: 0010
loses one hunk in ac_orbis_drm.c, and about 300 lines in 12 files that are
in mesa-build/mesa-ps4 (and so in every package) were in no patch at all.
This patch is exactly that difference, measured on 2026-11-07 against
1a59cc1 + 0001-0040 applied with `patch -p1 --forward` and rejects dropped.
What it carries:

- the allocation-failure diagnostics from the GTA IV out-of-memory work and
  the 1082 RADV allocation trace: PW_ORBIS_VA_FAIL (host-bookkeeping,
  replay-range, replay-conflict, window-exhausted), PW_ORBIS_MAP_FAIL
  stage=mprotect, PW_RADV_ALLOC_FAIL, RADV_GRAPHICS_PIPELINE_FAIL,
  RADV_BLIT2D_PIPELINE_FAIL, RADV_ALLOC_CMD_BUFFER, RADV_CS_FINALIZE,
  RADV_CMD_OOM and the command-stream list realloc failures;
- the Vulkan cursor overlay in wsi_orbis.c/.h that draws Wine's cursor image
  over the scan-out;
- 0010's lost hunk and smaller edits in the submit-trace and descriptor
  paths of ac_orbis_drm.c.

No behaviour change against shipped packages: this is what they were built
from.
---
